# Cloudflare Pages redirect rules.
#
# www.stackpick.net was serving the site directly with a 200 rather than
# redirecting, so both hostnames returned every page. The canonical tag points
# at the apex everywhere, which is usually enough for Google to consolidate,
# but a redirect removes the ambiguity instead of relying on it — and stops the
# www host accumulating its own crawl history.
#
# 301 is permanent: the apex is the canonical host and that is not going to
# change. :splat carries the rest of the path through.
https://www.stackpick.net/* https://stackpick.net/:splat 301!
